{"name":"Paarl","hex":"#864b36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Paarl","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in the Western Cape, South Africa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Paarl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paarl","blocks":[{"text":"Paarl is a town with 294,457 inhabitants in the Western Cape province of South Africa. It is the largest town in the Cape Winelands. Due to the growth of the Mbekweni township, it is now a de facto urban unit with Wellington. It is situated about 60 kilometres (37 mi) northeast of Cape Town in the Western Cape Province and is known for its scenic environment and viticulture and fruit-growing heritage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Paarl-monument.jpg/330px-Paarl-monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paarl","wikidata":"Q1018144"},{"title":"Paarl (House of Assembly of South Africa constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Paarl was a constituency in the Cape Province of South Africa, which existed from 1910 to 1994. The constituency covered a part of the Boland region centred on the town of Paarl. Throughout its existence it elected one member to the House of Assembly and one to the Cape Provincial Council."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/SA-1981-Paarl.png/330px-SA-1981-Paarl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paarl_(House_of_Assembly_of_South_Africa_constituency)","wikidata":"Q13035725"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Paarl-panorama_300dpi.jpg/500px-Paarl-panorama_300dpi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Paarl-panorama_300dpi.jpg/1280px-Paarl-panorama_300dpi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u